  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IMPLEMENTING SWEFCOMS TIGER CONSERVATION ACTION PLAN: CONSOLIDATING BASELINES AND ADDRESSING CRITICAL THREATS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE SCARCITY OF TIGER PREY IS CONSIDERED ONE OF THE KEY LIMITATIONS TO TIGER RECOVERY IN THE SOUTHERN WESTERN FOREST COMPLEX (SWEFCOM). THROUGH THIS PROJECT, PANTHERA PROPOSES TO ADDRESS THIS IN THE SALAKPRA CONSERVATION LANDSCAPE (SCL) THROUGH THREE DISTINCT LINES OF INTERVENTION. THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO (1) FILL SPATIAL AND TEMPORAL GAPS IN THE ECOLOGICAL MONITORING OF TIGERS AND PREY IN THE SCL (2) CONSOLIDATE THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROBLEM-ORIENTED APPROACH TO WILDLIFE PROTECTION IN THE LANDSCAPE AND IDENTIFY NON-ENFORCEMENT-BASED INTERVENTIONS AND (3) DEVELOP AN ACTION PLAN TO REDUCE AND REGULATE LIVESTOCK GRAZING PROTECTED AREAS IN THE NORTHERN SCL</narrative>
  </description>
